Rule 1 (dtypes of both input tensors must match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (inputs must have a floating-point or complex dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 3 (same number of dimensions and broadcast-compatible shapes if neither input is a scalar)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 7 (dimension equality for non-scalar input tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 8 (broadcasting compatibility of dimensions for non-scalar inputs)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) = 0 ∨ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
